  "details": "Currently the only way to programmatically update the social status, pronouns, or profile icon is using the unofficial API, which necessitates an awkward sign in mechanism, and doing so through the API doesn’t update them reliably on the local client. Having native OSC endpoints for setting them would be much more convenient. At the same time being able to receive updates could have some utility as well, but that’s more incidental to my particular use case\n\nThe primary motivation for this is for people with DID/OSDD who want to specify the fronting alter in their status, having a toggle on the avatar that triggers an OSC client to update the status and pronouns is much more convenient than doing it manually in the UI, especially with the new UI rework adding several more layers of nested menus and confirm buttons, making it even more cumbersome than before.",
